From 48cd85584cbe0dab778b14f0c2f9ba7c6c8a7d44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiziano Bacocco <tizbac2@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:24:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 072/123] fix(service): surface scheduled runs in Running Jobs,
 fix duplicate GUI instances, locale-proof state ACLs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three service-mode bugs:

Running machine backup never showed up: the Running Jobs tab lists
GET /backup/jobs, which only the two HTTP start handlers ever filled.
Scheduled runs and "Run now" start in runScheduledBackup instead, so the
service executed them invisibly. The service now hands the API server to
the App (SetJobReporter); runScheduledBackup registers an inline job,
dispatchProgress feeds it live progress, and a deferred close records the
outcome (idempotent, so a run that dies before its own OnComplete cannot
sit at "running" forever). The scheduler starts LAST so run-at-startup
jobs are visible from their first second. Applies to the Windows and the
Unix service; covered by TestRunScheduledBackupPublishesToJobReporter.

Duplicate GUI instances: after an elevated relaunch the Global mutex is
held at high integrity, and a medium-IL launch then gets ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED
from CreateMutex instead of ERROR_ALREADY_EXISTS. That error fell into
"allow launch on error", so every desktop launch opened another window.
ACCESS_DENIED now counts as "another instance exists" (someone does hold
the name): activate the existing window and exit. Activation also searches
the per-brand window title ("<Brand> v<version>") instead of only the
hardcoded default, so branded builds focus their own window instead of
appearing to do nothing.

Token/json configs locked everyone out: hardenWindowsACLs referenced
"SYSTEM"/"BUILTIN\Administrators" by English name and stripped
inheritance in the same icacls run. On a localized Windows the grant
fails, leaving the file with an EMPTY DACL — no user, not even SYSTEM
(owner keeps WRITE_DAC but no file access), could read or write the
api-token or any JSON config. Grants now use SIDs (*S-1-5-18,
*S-1-5-32-544) in their own invocation BEFORE the inheritance strip, so a
failure can only stay over-permissive, never unreachable, and icacls
output is logged instead of discarded. api.setTokenFileACL builds its
trustees from SIDs as well, with file-specific access masks.

Upstream: tizbac/proxmoxbackupclient_go@44969cf1ef181528b19e17ae21d0a578a12c91cd
